From 9e2a3a68b1977ab615d7ae95f30d3e17924cca4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Add routine, go-to and together cards, with a routine
 editor

A routine is a pattern defined relative to where it starts (forward and
left steps, curves through a control point), stored once under
auto.routines and placed by routine cards at a named point with a
facing, an optional mirror and an exit point. It exports as
kit.routine with the pattern placed on the field as a Path local, and
previews until its condition, timeout or the pattern's end, then drives
to the exit. The card editor checks the placement against the walls and
keep-out zones and hosts the routine editor: a steps table, a pattern
canvas with draggable points, the end condition, timeout and actions.

goTo drives straight to a named point within a distance or runs its
fallback cards (kit.goTo); together runs cards at once until all or the
first are done (kit.together). The sample now uses all three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
